{"name":"Tuatara","hex":"#454642","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tuatara","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reptile, Sphenodon punctatus, native to New Zealand, that resembles a lizard and is the only surviving specimen of the order Rhynchocephalia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tuatara"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tuatara","blocks":[{"text":"The tuatara is a species of reptile endemic to New Zealand. Despite its close resemblance to lizards, it is the only extant member of a distinct lineage, the previously highly diverse order Rhynchocephalia. The name tuatara is derived from the Māori language and means \"peaks on the back\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Tuatara_%285205719005%29.jpg/330px-Tuatara_%285205719005%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuatara"},{"title":"Tuatara (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Tuatara is an American, Seattle-based instrumental music group, featuring members of R.E.M., The Minus 5, Critters Buggin, The Chills and the Screaming Trees."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuatara_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png/500px-World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png/1280px-World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png/500px-World.distribution.rhynchocephalia.colour_contrast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.w